---
description: Writing and code conventions for my design projects
alwaysApply: true
---

Writing and copy:
- Never use em dashes. Use a period, comma, parens, or colon instead.
- Peer-level tone, casual and direct. No mentor-speak, no "let's", no hedging.
- No over-explaining. Lead with the answer.

Code:
- Tailwind utility classes only, no custom CSS unless unavoidable.
- Functional React components with TypeScript.
- Match Linear, Vercel, Supabase visual conventions: neutral palette, tight spacing, restrained color use.
- Lead with visual output when building UI. Show the component, don't describe options.
